            <ArticleTitle>New NIH Regulations Say Most Basic Human Brain Research Is a Clinical Trial.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>14-16</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0896-6273(17)30789-4</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.neuron.2017.09.001</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>New NIH definitions classify virtually all human brain and behavioral research as clinical trials. The new definitions will change regulatory, reporting, and funding schemes for noninvasive studies such as neuroimaging. Resulting burdens threaten the viability of basic biobehavioral science research.</AbstractText>
